      "note": "Pricing page: \"Azure Container Apps Express and Sandboxes follow the same pay-per-second pricing as Consumption Plan\" = $0.000024/vCPU-s + $0.000003/GiB-s (eastus, Retail API). Billed only while Running; stopped = no CPU/memory. Tiers per docs: XS 0.25c/0.5GB/20GB, S 0.5/1/20, M 1/2/20 (default), L 2/4/40, XL 4/8/80. GA blog says XS disk is 5 GB. Basis verified 2026-09-28: Idle: \"Auto-suspend: Suspend an idle sandbox after a configurable timeout. A sandbox becomes idle when it has no ingress (incoming) traffic, no code execution (via execute API), no interactive shell sessions, and no file operations.\" ; \"You pay no CPU or memory fees when sandboxes are stopped.\" (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/container-apps/sandboxes-overview). Metered on the tier allocation (alloc). Merged 2026-09-28 with the former custom-size regime (same meters: tiers are exactly vCPU x $0.0864 + GiB x $0.0108): GA blog \"Programmatically you can go up to 16 vCPU with 32 GB of memory and a 320 GB disk\"; 8/16 and 16/32 added as representative programmatic sizes (1:2 ratio; disk for 8/16 not published).",
